      {
        "id": 131595,
        "name": "Silverleaf",
        "username": "Silverleaf",
        "avatar_template": "/user_avatar/forums.greaterthangames.com/silverleaf/{size}/2332_2.png",
        "created_at": "2015-02-17T05:18:21.000Z",
        "cooked": "<aside class=\"quote group-playtesters\" data-username=\"Reckless\">\n<div class=\"title\">\n<div class=\"quote-controls\"></div>\n<img loading=\"lazy\" alt=\"\" width=\"24\" height=\"24\" src=\"https://forums.greaterthangames.com/user_avatar/forums.greaterthangames.com/reckless/48/2467_2.png\" class=\"avatar\"> Reckless:</div>\n<blockquote>\n<div><b>Silverleaf wrote:</b><br><blockquote>Reckless wrote:<blockquote>\nAnd The Dreamer is too young to have a fully developed sexuality.\n</blockquote>\nNot fully developed, but many six-year-olds are aware of their preferences and are clearly identifying with a particular gender by that age.\n</blockquote></div>\nI was referring more to sexual preference, but that is a fair observation. \n</blockquote>\n</aside>\n<p>So was I. Not necessarily in terms of sexual activity (although some sexual activity such as genital touching, \"playing doctor\" and masturbation is common and normal), but in terms of knowing what \"flavour\" of partner they'd like to have in the future.</p>\n<p>There's a lot of truth in the trope of the teenager who finally plucks up the courage to come out to their family after years of angst and gets the response, \"We've known for years.\"</p>",
